# Build context for every image. All three Dockerfiles use the repository root
# as their context, because the pnpm workspace only resolves as a whole.
#
# A denylist rather than an allowlist on purpose: an allowlist that forgets a
# file the build needs fails loudly, but it also has to be updated every time a
# config file is added, and the failure then looks like a broken build rather
# than a stale ignore file.

# Version control and CI. Never in an image: .git carries every previous
# revision of every secret that was ever committed and then removed.
.git
.gitignore
.github

# Installed per-stage inside the image from the lockfile. Copying the host's
# would defeat layer caching and can carry native modules built for the host.
node_modules
**/node_modules

# Build output. Rebuilt inside the image; a stale local copy silently wins.
dist
**/dist
.next
**/.next
out
**/out
*.tsbuildinfo
**/*.tsbuildinfo

# Local environment. These hold real credentials.
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# Local runtime state. Uploads live in a volume, not in the image.
backend/uploads
coverage
**/coverage
*.log
test-results
playwright-report

# Not part of any build.
documentation
scripts
infrastructure/kubernetes
infrastructure/terraform
README.md
**/.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
